    "essence": "The art of being truly heard and truly listening.",
    "light": "Communication is a bridge built plank by plank between two inner worlds. At its best it's honest and kind at once. In plain terms: saying what's real, listening for what's underneath, and repairing when words go wrong. Good communication makes people feel less alone.",
    "shadow": "In excess, communication can become a need to be heard at all costs: over-explaining, filling every silence, winning rather than understanding. Words multiply while connection thins.",
    "void": "When it goes missing, things are felt but not said, and distance grows in the gaps. Silence can be a habit learned in homes where speaking up wasn't safe. The unspoken is often what most needs air.",
    "whole": "Presence steadies communication. Listening fully before answering, and letting silence breathe, turn talk into true meeting.",
