    "essence": "The aliveness of not-knowing, and leaning in.",
    "light": "Curiosity is the lantern held up to every unexplored path. It asks why, and what if, and tell me more. Plainly: a genuine interest in learning, exploring and understanding, whether that's people, ideas or the world around you. It turns strangers into stories and problems into puzzles, and keeps a mind growing long after it could have stopped.",
    "shadow": "Too much, and curiosity scatters: always the next thing, never staying long enough to go deep. It can also cross into intrusion, wanting to know more than someone wants to share.",
    "void": "Without curiosity, life can settle into certainty and routine that feel safe but dull. Sometimes curiosity was punished, or life got too heavy for it. It tends to return when there's a little more room to breathe.",
