    "shadow": "Too much, and honesty becomes a blade. Truth delivered without care can wound, and \"I'm just being honest\" can excuse cruelty. Not every thought needs to be spoken, and not every moment is the right one.",
    "void": "Without honesty, small untruths gather like fog. You might tell people what they want to hear, or avoid facing what you know inside. Dishonesty usually starts as protection. Speaking one small truth can clear more air than you'd expect.",
    "whole": "Compassion softens honesty's edge. Truth told with care is heard; truth thrown is defended against. Kind honesty is the most useful kind.",
