    "light": "Presence is the still point at the centre of the turning wheel. It's arriving in your own life: tasting the food, hearing the person, feeling your feet on the ground. In plain terms: giving your full attention to this moment, instead of living in worry, memory or a screen. Presence doesn't change what's happening; it changes whether you're there for it.",
    "shadow": "Taken too far, \"just be here\" can become a way to avoid the future or the past. Plans, consequences and old wounds get set aside in the name of the present moment. Stillness becomes a way around things rather than through them.",
    "void": "Without presence, life happens somewhere else: in worry, memory or a screen. Days blur. That absence often protects you from something the present holds. Gently coming back, even for a breath, is the practice.",
    "whole": "Responsibility keeps presence grounded. Being here now includes caring for what comes next. Together they let you live fully in the moment without abandoning your life.",
