    "light": "Wonder is looking up at the night sky and feeling both tiny and part of everything. It's the gasp at a sunrise, the child's \"whoa\" at a beetle. In plain terms: a sense of amazement and awe at life's mystery and beauty. Wonder reminds you that the world is bigger than your worries.",
    "shadow": "Too much, and wonder can drift into escapism: always gazing at the stars and never at the ground. Life's practical needs can slip away while you're lost in the marvel.",
